From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Test the DateTime::Locale 1.35 C alias explicitly

DateTime::Locale 1.35 canonicalizes C as en-US; 1.00-1.34 used
en-US-POSIX. The original test assumes every version at least 1.00
returns the older identifier. Keep its concrete locale assertion and
all 20 default assertions, adjusting only the version-dependent expected
constant. The fixed SP3 provider is 1.35; local 1.25 retains its branch.

---
 t/02_main.t | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/t/02_main.t b/t/02_main.t
--- a/t/02_main.t
+++ b/t/02_main.t
@@ -63,2 +63,3 @@
-	# DateTime::Locale version 1.00 changes "C" to "en-US-POSIX".
-	my $expected = eval { DateTime::Locale->VERSION(1) } ? "en-US-POSIX" : "C";
+	# DateTime::Locale 1.35 changes "C" from "en-US-POSIX" to "en-US".
+	my $expected = eval { DateTime::Locale->VERSION(1.35) } ? "en-US"
+	             : eval { DateTime::Locale->VERSION(1) } ? "en-US-POSIX" : "C";
